JH <no@email.com> wrote:
> I was thinking about doing an extinsionist wizard, just because I love W's
> and am looking for an excuse to ascend another one :).  I was wondering, how
> can you tell when the work is done?  Do you just cast create monster and
> wait for nothing to happen?  Also, how do you deal with the memory loss of
> spells? (if your god is happy with you and gives you a spellbook, will he
> give you one that you've been given/had before, but no longer have in your
> inventory?)

Between polypiling, using magic markers, praying, and random monster stuff,
you shouldn't have any problems with spellbooks.  Be sure to conduct your
killing frenzy on an altar, sacrificing every so often, and praying when you
can.  You'll get crowned fairly soon, but it's an almost inexhaustible
source of spellbooks even so.

The generally accepted way to go extinctionist is to pick a nice level with
an altar in the main dungeon, cast create monster 'til you're blue in the 
face (or, really, until nothing shows up), go up to level 1, cast CM until
nothing shows up, then dive down, casting CM until nothing shows up down
on every level down to the VS.  The places where lots will happen are
your choice of main level, the Oracle level, and the VotD, although some
critters should show up on just about every second level, IIRC.

Be prepared to kill 120 archons.  It's an evil task.

Going extinctionist takes *forever*.  I did it, once.  It took about five
weeks, real time.  

